that I referenced earlier.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.050
We have capabilities like
dual-ended QoS and last mile

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:03.370
awareness, so that if there are
changing bandwidth conditions,

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.710
our network can
adapt to that, again

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.040
in the interests of delivering
that better user experience.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.100
And then we've also got
unique capabilities,

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.170
like sub-second
failover of links.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.660
And so if customers
in remote locations,

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.850
in the case of
retail, they're using

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:23.890
